{
  "dom_id": "question-181974",
  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "If $A={1,2,3}$ and $B={x,y},$ which of the following elements belong to $(B\\times B)\\times A?$\n\nI. $(x,y,1)$\n\nII. $((x,x),1)$\n\nIII. $((y,x),2)$",
  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $B\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${x,y}$ with ${x,y},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14123139/assets/5af389ab817ce509519af7a3c1a5fdbb583d8e13859b9aa3b6166958f81e3040.png)\n\nHence, the set $B\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nB\\times B={(x,x),(x,y),(y,x),(y,y)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|B\\times B|=|B|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\n(B\\times B)\\times A\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $B\\times B$ and $A,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14123139/assets/dae7febad357be8d9f000c9dc7abfbe97fda34e3e9ff0b0e8ab0289e3c4e782a.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|(B\\times B)\\times A|=|B\\times B|\\cdot |A|=4\\cdot 3=12.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $((x,x),1)$ and $((y,x),2)$ are in $(B\\times B)\\times A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
  "answer_fields_complete": true,
  "result": "Correct",
